Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:15:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?radio=5Fplanner:=20never=20strand=20an=20enqueu?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ed=20ASAP=20task=20=E2=80=94=20clamp=20past-due=20starts,=20fix?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20rank/hook=20index=20clobber?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two defects could silently drop a registered task, stranding the submit
that enqueued it (bench 2026-09-02: TX submit returned OK, the chip never
left standby, the task was later released with zero packets aired, and the
host TX watchdog burned its full retry budget on the wedged slot before an
MCU cold reset was the only escape):

1. rp_task_arbiter aborted a high-priority ASAP task whose start_time had
   slipped into the past (delay < 0). ASAP means 'as soon as possible' —
   the start is now clamped and the task launches; only SCHEDULED tasks
   (genuinely stale work) keep the abort.

2. rp_task_select_next's low-priority ASAP delay loop wrote
   rp->tasks[i].start_time_ms using the RANKING POSITION i instead of the
   hook id rankings[i] — whenever the ranking vector was not the identity
   map, the start_time of an unrelated registered task was clobbered,
   corrupting its schedule and feeding defect 1.
---
 .../radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c         | 26 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
index 48cd248..af70c88 100644
--- a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
+++ b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
@@ -799,7 +799,23 @@ static void rp_task_arbiter( radio_planner_t* rp, const char* caller_func_name )
         // Case where the high priority task is in the past, error case
         if( delay < 0 )
         {  // The high priority task is in the past, error case
-            if( rp->priority_task.state != RP_TASK_STATE_RUNNING )
+            if( rp->priority_task.state == RP_TASK_STATE_ASAP )
+            {
+                // SuperLexicon patch 0006: an ASAP task whose start_time
+                // slipped into the past must be CLAMPED and launched, not
+                // silently aborted — ASAP means "as soon as possible", and
+                // dropping the task here strands the submit that enqueued
+                // it: the submitter waits on a transaction the planner
+                // will never run (bench 2026-09-02: TX submit OK, chip
+                // never left standby, task released with zero packets
+                // aired — the host TX watchdog then burned its whole
+                // retry budget on a wedged slot). SCHEDULED tasks keep
+                // the abort: they are genuinely stale work.
+                rp->tasks[rp->priority_task.hook_id].start_time_ms = now;
+                rp->priority_task.start_time_ms                    = now;
+                delay                                              = 0;
+            }
+            else if( rp->priority_task.state != RP_TASK_STATE_RUNNING )
             {
                 rp->stats.rp_error++;
                 SMTC_MODEM_HAL_RP_TRACE_PRINTF( " RP: ERROR - delay #%d - hook #%d\n", delay,
@@ -1170,7 +1186,13 @@ static uint8_t rp_task_select_next( radio_planner_t* rp, const uint32_t now )
         rank = rp->rankings[i];
         if( rp->tasks[rank].state == RP_TASK_STATE_ASAP )
         {
-            rp->tasks[i].start_time_ms = hook_time_to_exe_tmp;
+            // SuperLexicon patch 0006: index the task by RANK (the hook id
+            // at this ranking position), not by the loop index — the old
+            // `rp->tasks[i]` clobbered the start_time of an UNRELATED
+            // registered task whenever the ranking vector was not the
+            // identity map (multiple tasks registered), corrupting its
+            // schedule and feeding the arbiter's past-task abort.
+            rp->tasks[rank].start_time_ms = hook_time_to_exe_tmp;
         }
     }
     return RP_SOMETHING_TO_DO;
